
- decision auditability

:: core concepts ::

decision auditability (means) the ability to reconstruct why a system produced a given output
    "                (requires) inputs, rules, model version, data-as-known-then
    "                (requires) stable identifiers and immutable history
reproducibility (contrast) getting the same answer given same inputs
explainability (contrast) human-interpretable reasoning for an output
auditability (broader than) explainability — includes provenance and timing

provenance (means) lineage of a datum: where it came from, how it was transformed
lineage (related) dataset-level provenance in data platforms
time-travel (enables) "re-run the decision as of time T"
bitemporality (enables) distinguishing "what we knew then" from "what was true then"

:: regulatory drivers ::

GDPR Art. 22 (requires) right to meaningful information about automated decisions
EU AI Act 2024 (requires) logging, traceability for high-risk AI systems
SR 11-7 from US Fed (requires) model risk management, documented decision trails
BCBS 239 (requires) risk data aggregation with full lineage
MiFID II (requires) reconstruction of trading decisions to the millisecond
SOX (requires) audit trails over financial reporting systems
NYDFS Part 500 (requires) cybersecurity event reconstruction
HIPAA (requires) access and modification audit trails for PHI

:: architectural approaches ::

event sourcing (role) append-only event log as source of truth
     "         (enables) replay to reconstruct any past state
CQRS (related) separates write-model events from read-model projections
bitemporal DB (role) system+valid time natively support as-of replay
immutable ledgers (example) XTDB, Datomic, Kafka-as-database patterns
feature stores (role) store model inputs at inference time for later audit
model registries (role) MLflow, SageMaker, W&B — version model artifacts
decision logs (pattern) record inputs, model_version, output, timestamp per call

:: ML/AI-specific concerns ::

LLMs (problem) non-determinism via temperature, sampling
  "  (mitigation) log seeds, prompts, tool calls, retrieved context
  "  (problem) training data provenance often opaque
RAG (problem) retrieved chunks change as index changes — snapshot them
drift (problem) feature or label drift invalidates prior decisions retroactively
shadow deployment (practice) log proposed decisions without acting on them

:: industry & research trends ::

trend (item) decision intelligence platforms like Palantir, Quantexa, Decision Systems Intl
trend (item) OpenLineage standard for data lineage across tools
trend (item) OpenTelemetry extending into semantic conventions for AI/LLM spans
trend (item) policy-as-code: OPA, Cedar — auditable decision engines
trend (item) rules engines re-emerging — Drools, Clara — for auditable logic
trend (item) "glass-box" ML: interpretable models preferred in regulated sectors
trend (item) differential privacy vs. auditability tension
research (item) causal inference frameworks for counterfactual audits
research (item) zk-proofs for auditing without revealing inputs

:: challenges, tensions ::

tension (item) GDPR erasure vs. immutable audit logs
tension (item) log volume vs. retention cost
tension (item) privacy of inputs vs. need for replay
tension (item) system-time-only time travel misses retroactive corrections
tension (item) vendor black-box foundation models limit full auditability
tension (item) "audit theatre" — logging without anyone able to replay

:: key voices ::

Cathy O'Neil (work) Weapons of Math Destruction — algorithmic accountability
Rich Hickey (concept) "place-oriented programming" as anti-pattern; values over time
Mark Burgess (concept) Promise Theory — commitments as units of audit
Pat Helland (paper) "Immutability Changes Everything"
Martin Fowler (concept) event sourcing patterns

